# Docker build context excludes for the IrieFishmongers monorepo.
# Build context is always the repository ROOT (all three Dockerfiles resolve
# npm workspaces + packages/* from here). Exclude host-generated artifacts that
# are regenerated inside the image, anything secret, and clutter not needed by
# the workspace build or Prisma generation. Do NOT exclude package manifests,
# lockfile, source, tsconfig*, next.config, or backend/prisma (schema +
# migrations are required for `prisma generate`).

# Dependencies — reinstalled in-image via `npm ci`
**/node_modules

# Build output — regenerated in-image (nest build / next build)
**/dist
**/build
**/.next
**/out
**/.turbo
.turbo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Test / coverage output
**/coverage

# Secrets & local env — MUST NOT enter the build context. Required public
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* values are passed as build args, never via copied env files.
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Version control / CI metadata
.git
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github

# Expo / React Native local caches (mobile app scaffolds)
**/.expo
**/.expo-shared

# Logs
**/*.log

# Editor / OS clutter
.vscode
.idea
**/.DS_Store
**/Thumbs.db
~$*

# Agent / local tooling state
.claude
.nvmrc
.prettierignore
.prettierrc.json
eslint.config.mjs

# Docs and non-code project folders not needed to build images
docs
readme.md
**/*.md
Irie-Fishmongers-Logo.jpg
Personal info
git-repository
infrastructure
Startup instructions.md
